A bare pattern name like \code{"stripe"} is resolved as follows:
\enumerate{
\item If the user has set a preference with \code{\link[=prefer_pattern]{prefer_pattern()}} then the preferred pattern.
\item If exactly one owner (the user, \code{{gridpattern}}, or a loaded package) has a pattern with that name
then that pattern.
Patterns set by the user with the (legacy) \code{ggpattern_geometry_funcs} / \code{ggpattern_array_funcs} options
are owned by the user.
If the user has more than one pattern with that name (from \code{register_pattern()} and/or the options)
an error is thrown asking them to remove all but one of them
(since they share the same qualified name \code{"R_GlobalEnv::name"} a preference can't choose between them).
\item Otherwise there is a conflict and an error is thrown, asking for either a qualified \code{"owner::name"}
or a \code{\link[=prefer_pattern]{prefer_pattern()}} preference.
In particular, a user pattern with the same name as a builtin \code{{gridpattern}} pattern
does not mask the builtin pattern without a preference.
